According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, the global Polypropylene Thread Market was valued at USD 2.922 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 3.967 billion by 2034, reflecting a CAGR of 4.0% over the forecast horizon. Polypropylene thread is a synthetic filament produced from propylene polymers, offering high tensile strength, chemical resistance, low moisture absorption and lightweight characteristics. Its resistance to mildew and UV radiation and its cost advantages support applications across textiles, industrial sewing, packaging, geotextiles, ropes, fishing nets and agriculture.
